; MOTT -- a descent after NetHack, for COOL8, in CoolAction!
;
; The Amulet of Mott lies twelve levels down. Fetch it, and climb back
; to the sun. The game is Rogue's and NetHack's -- rooms on a three by
; three grid joined by corridors, a map remembered as it is seen, levels
; that stay as they were left, monsters by NetHack's own numbers and a pet
; at your side -- drawn in DawnLike's tiles, by DragonDePlatino on
; DawnBringer's palette (CC-BY 4.0), which tools/mkmott.py cuts from
; assets/dawnlike/ into assets/mott/.
;
; **A cell of the dungeon is 16 x 16, four tiles**, so the screen shows
; twenty cells by thirteen of a level forty by twenty-four, and follows
; the hero across it. Mode 2's tiles have no transparency, so a creature
; or an item is drawn onto the floor by the generator, and each band of
; the dungeon -- its floor, its walls, its stairs -- is a file of four
; pattern banks on MOTT's drive, streamed into VRAM on the stairs.
;
; **What is in view is in DawnBringer's sixteen; what is remembered is in
; the same sixteen dimmed** -- palette bank 0 and 1 -- so the map fades as
; the hero leaves it, and no tile is drawn twice for it.
;
; **Levels persist.** The current one is in memory; the others are parked
; in VRAM above the pattern banks, a slot each, monsters and all, and come
; back as they were.
;
; **The fighting is NetHack's**: a blow lands when 1 + the hero's bonus +
; the target's armour class + the hero's level + the weapon's enchantment
; beats a twenty-sided die, and a monster's when 10 + the hero's armour
; class + its level does; its attacks, its speed, how often it appears and
; how deep are monst.c's. Experience is NetHack's doubling ladder.
;
; **The things are NetHack's too**: its weapons, armour, potions, scrolls,
; wands, rings and amulets by objects.c's numbers, blessed, uncursed or
; cursed as mksobj() makes them, and the potions, scrolls, wands and rings
; under appearances each game shuffles -- a pink potion, a scroll labeled
; ZELGO MER -- until they are used or identified.
;
; Milestones 1 to 5: the dungeon, walking, doors, stairs, what is seen and
; remembered; the monsters, the fighting, the three heroes, their levels,
; the pet; the things and what they do; traps and secret doors, fountains,
; altars and prayer, Elbereth, shops; the mines' caves and town, the
; Oracle's Delphi, Sokoban. docs/14-demos.md has the plan.
;
; **Its messages are on its drive**: a #"text" is a number here and a
; string in MOTT.STR, which the compiler writes and Str() reads, as the
; names are records in MNAMES.DAT that NameRec() reads (D109, D110).
;
; Keys: the cursor keys, the keypad or h j k l y u b n move -- two cursor
; keys held together go diagonally -- and moving into a monster attacks
; it, into the pet changes places; walking into a door opens it; > and <
; take the stairs, and Enter the stairs you stand on; . rests and s
; searches. As in NetHack: i the pack, , picks up, d drops, w wields, W
; wears, T takes off, P puts on, R removes, q drinks, r reads, z zaps, t
; throws, f fires daggers, : looks here, \ lists what is known, Z casts
; the Wizard's force bolt, p pays, E engraves, # takes a long command
; (#pray, #chat), ? shows the keys. Ctrl+R draws the screen again; Esc asks to
; quit.

CONST MDRIVE = 9                     ; MOTT's drive: its program and its themes
CONST PAT_BASE = $1000               ; the four pattern banks, $1000-$8FFF of VRAM
CONST SLOT_BASE = $9000              ; a parked level a slot, above them
CONST SLOT_SIZE = 1536

; the level, and the window on it
CONST LW = 40
CONST LH = 24
CONST NCELL = 960
CONST VW = 20
CONST VH = 13
CONST VTOP = 2                       ; the tile row the window starts on
CONST MAXDEPTH = 12
CONST MAXMON = 20                    ; monsters on a level at once, the pet among them

; a cell's byte: what is there in the low four bits, and four flags
CONST K_ROCK = 0
CONST K_WALL = 1
CONST K_FLOOR = 2
CONST K_CORR = 3
CONST K_DOORC = 4
CONST K_DOORO = 5
CONST K_DOORWAY = 6
CONST K_UP = 7
CONST K_DOWN = 8
CONST K_SDOOR = 9                    ; a door that looks like the wall until it is found
CONST K_SCORR = 10                   ; a corridor that looks like rock until it is found
CONST K_FOUNTAIN = 11
CONST K_ALTAR = 12                   ; 12 lawful, 13 neutral, 14 chaotic
CONST F_TRAP = 16                    ; a trap is on the cell: the traps' list says which
CONST F_LIT = 32                     ; a floor lit, so its room is seen whole
CONST F_SEEN = 64                    ; seen once, and remembered
CONST F_VIS = 128                    ; in view now

; a monster's state bits
CONST S_LIVE = 1
CONST S_PET = 2
CONST S_ANGRY = 4                    ; bitten by the pet: it bites back

; the objects
